Fix: false pre-opening detection in recovered Sun Valley code
File: recovery/src/booking/sunValley.cs   (only this file changed)

ROOT CAUSE
  Open/closed was decided solely from the calendar date-cell `title` attribute read from
  //*[@id='A<yyyymmdd>']/a  (or B<...>), via BookingDiagnostics.Classify():
      title.Contains("잔여팀")            -> SlotsAvailable
      title.Contains("마감")              -> Closed
      title.Contains("오픈전") ...        -> NotOpenYet  -> refresh branch
      else                                -> Unknown     -> refresh branch
  Sun Valley served title="오픈전입니다" for a date whose real reserve rows
  (.btn.btn-res) were already present and bookable, so the macro refreshed past
  open tee times. The title is advisory, not authoritative; the authoritative signal
  is the presence of the .btn.btn-res rows the booking flow (find()/compare()) consumes.
  URL / time-window conditions were not involved. No inference from log text.

CHANGE (minimal): probe the real reserve rows before the pre-opening refresh branch;
if rows exist, classify OPEN regardless of title. Bounded retries + diagnostic
no-submit mode unchanged.

